# Copy to `.env` in this folder (same name, no `.example`).
# `.env` is gitignored — never commit it, never paste keys into GitHub/issues/PRs.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Or run `npm run meal-parse` from `app/` once; it creates `.env` from this file if missing.
#
# `meal_parse_server.py` also loads this folder’s `dev.env` then `.env` with python-dotenv,
# so keys apply when you run `uvicorn` directly (IDE, etc.), not only via `npm run meal-parse`.

# Required for USDA (override DEMO_KEY from dev.env if you hit rate limits)
# USDA_API_KEY=

# Required for ingredient + portion extraction (meal-parse “smart” path).
# `npm run meal-parse` also loads ../../realtime-proxy/.env if present (same key as voice proxy).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional
# MEAL_PARSE_OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# POST /meal-parse/debug — off by default here; dev.env sets MEAL_PARSE_DEBUG=1 for npm run meal-parse.
# MEAL_PARSE_DEBUG=0
#
# --- Render (free web service) ---
# Deploy with repo-root render.yaml (Blueprint) or a manual Web Service with root
# api-testing/USDA-API, build pip install -r requirements.txt, start
#   uvicorn meal_parse_server:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT
# Set USDA_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, and MEAL_PARSE_DEBUG=0 in the Render dashboard.
# CORS: set MEAL_PARSE_CORS_ORIGINS to your Netlify site origin (comma-separated if several).
